# The waystation: a settlement at a crossroads, at the size decisions.md entry 007 asked for.
#
# Radius 24 — 49 hexes and 85 m across, eighteen hundred tiles — so a rifle at 55 m and a sentry
# at 45 m have somewhere to be different from each other. Open ground with a walled compound on
# the main road, a stream crossed by one bridge, a barn, a pair of cottages, a ridge, a
# watchtower and two stands of trees.
#
# ---- what the ground offers a mission -------------------------------------------------------
#
# This map used to carry a mission in its header, in prose, because there was nowhere else to put
# one. There is now: content/missions/waystation.hexmission, which holds the deployments, the way
# off, the objective and the clock, and is the only copy of them. Entry 047. What stays here is
# the part that is about the ground, because the ground is what this file is.
#
# The sentry's post outside the west gate looks straight down the west road through the gap in
# the trees, so the road is a queue and the fields either side of it are the approach. The stream
# is too deep to wade, and the two ways over it are the bridge, in full view of the gate, and the
# ford below the compound, slow and loud and unwatched. The drain under the south wall, five
# hexes from the ford, is the way into the compound that nobody is watching. The barn and the
# tower are outside earshot of the compound (entry 037), so anything that happens on the roof
# does not reach them unless somebody says so.

map Waystation

# Kit the built-ins do not have. A hedge you can push through but not see through; the
# planking of the bridge, which is louder underfoot than the road either side of it; and the
# stream itself, which is too deep to wade. The first twelve matches fought here had everybody
# wading straight across and nobody using the bridge, which made the one crossing on the map a
# decoration. Now it is a crossing.
profile hedge height 1.5 cover light passable opaque destructible
ground boardwalk cost 0 noise 1.4
ground deep noise 2 impassable

# ---- ground ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

fill disc 0,0 r 24 grass
fill disc -10,6 r 3 rubble
fill disc 6,-16 r 2 shallow_water

# A ridge, high enough that getting up it is a climb, with one cut path on the road side.
fill disc -12,-6 r 3 h 1.5
stairs -8,-6 -9,-6

# The stream runs north-west to south-east, west of the compound, and cuts the map in two. Two
# ways over it: the bridge, where the main road crosses in full view of the west gate, and a
# ford below the compound, slow and loud and watched by nobody.
fill line -20,24 to 4,-24 deep
fill line -24,0 to 24,0 gravel
fill line 10,-24 to 10,14 gravel
fill hex -8,0 boardwalk
fill hex -6,-4 shallow_water

# A line of trees along the field boundary west of the stream, with the road running through
# a gap in it. Without it the west road was a firing lane: in twelve matches out of twelve the
# rifleman on the road shot the sentry at the gate from 35 m on the second round, before
# anybody on either side had so much as a suspicion. The road is still a queue; the fields on
# either side of it are now an approach.
wall screen line -12,-2 to -12,5 ne se
breach -12,0 ne se

# ---- the compound -------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Paved inside, a solid wall all round, a gate at each end of the main road, and a drain under
# the south wall that somebody small and patient could crawl through.
fill disc 0,0 r 4 floor
enclose solid disc 0,0 r 4
breach 4,0 ne
breach -4,0 sw
link crawl -1,-3 -1,-4

# Sandbags outside both gates, covering the road. The west line runs across the road itself, so
# the sentry standing behind it has half cover from the way we are coming and traffic vaults.
wall low hexes 5,-1 5,1 ne
wall low hexes -5,-1 -5,0 -5,1 sw

# The house in the middle: a door on the south side, a flat roof with a parapet, and a ladder
# up from the yard on the east.
enclose solid disc 0,1 r 1
breach 0,0 s
fill disc 0,1 r 1 layer 1 h 3
enclose railing disc 0,1 r 1 layer 1
ladder 2,1@0 1,1@1

# ---- outbuildings -------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The barn: head-high walls you could climb, and one door on the west.
fill disc 14,-6 r 2 floor
enclose high disc 14,-6 r 2
breach 12,-6 sw

# Two cottages on the west bank, sharing a wall, door facing the road. They used to stand in
# the stream, which nobody noticed until the stream stopped being wadable.
fill hexes -14,6 -14,7 -13,6 floor
enclose solid hexes -14,6 -14,7 -13,6
wall solid hex -14,6 n
breach -13,6 se

# The watchtower: a platform four metres up, railed, ladder only.
fill hex 16,-14 layer 1 h 4
enclose railing hex 16,-14 layer 1
ladder 16,-14@0 16,-14@1

# Ruins by the east road: the odd wall left standing.
chord high 20,-9 0-2
chord low 20,-8 1-3
chord low 21,-10 3-5

# ---- cover in the open --------------------------------------------------------------------

# Two stands of trees, dense enough to hide in and walk through.
wall screen disc 14,6 r 2 all
wall screen disc -6,-14 r 1 all

# Hedgerows along the field boundaries north of the road.
wall hedge line 2,6 to 2,14 nw sw
wall hedge line -14,14 to -6,14 n
